# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the SHIP-3 gates (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of
# tp4/ship-3 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Templates only: no tag is pushed from the
# branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the pass rule. ONE IMAGE: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-3 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed commit
# (sed -i 's/tp4-ship-3/<tag>/' *.env). The ship profile and its approved waiver are the ship pack's, byte for byte. Nothing here stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# SR (STOP): the four-card platform replay of the PRODUCTION image: the node agent's serving sequence in a copy of its container running the THIN LAYER built on the B0
# (SHIP-3) image (C2_PLATFORM_IMAGE=local:thin-layer: the step reads the image name from a file the operator writes on the runner; it is never committed). The replay sets
# no profile, so it boots the ship profile BY THE IMAGE DEFAULT, which is why it needs the baked B0 image. THE RECORDED SOURCE IMAGE: as in the ship pack's SR, the replay
# copies the node agent's container from a tracked record (scripts/ci/references/c2-serving, the step's --source) and needs that image present on the rig host
# (c2_platform_replay.source_problem); when the step reports 'the source image ... is not on this host', the operator pulls it first - the image name stays out of this
# file. READ the vLLM subprocess log: '[QWEN-C2] profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic: vLLM argv', the OWNER TRAFFIC WAIVER line, the P150x4
# mesh, admission passed with no UNQUALIFIED admission line and no 262k evidence waiver, prefix installed, the Lever N install and warm lines, the parked build line, every
# op-fusion lever's engaged line, 'toolcall whitespace: armed' and 'toolcall whitespace: installed on', the :tt alias before and after the restart, and no kill-switch line
# (no levern.off, prefix-reuse.off or parked.off left on the hub). PASS: 'PLATFORM_REPLAY passed=True'. The replay turns the session cap off; the cap is read live after the
# deploy. The replay step has no telemetry sidecar. Measured basis: 25 minutes. Duration (estimate): 30 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset replay
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-3
C2_PLATFORM_IMAGE=local:thin-layer
C2_REPLAY_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic
C2_BOX_MINUTES=60
